     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Blocking h1_1:pivot and h2_1:pivot makes the target unreachable. One block is not enough. Blocking h1_1:pivot removes h3_1:escalate. It also removes h3_0:escalate, because that AND step needs both h1_1 and h1_0. With h3_0 gone, h5_1:access and h4_0:access fall. Blocking h2_1:pivot removes h3_2:reach, h5_2:pivot and h4_2:access. Now h5_0:reach has no live parent (h4_0, h4_2 and h3_1 are all gone), so all three parents of crown:obtain are cut. A single block cannot work because two attack paths share no blockable step: edge0 -> h2_1 -> h3_2 -> h5_2 -> crown, and edge0 -> h1_1 -> h3_1 -> h5_0 -> crown.\"}"
